contentText:
Dave Matthews , Trey Anastasio and Chris Stapleton all performed at Manhattan&#8217;s Cipriani on Tuesday night (Sept. 15) — but at the annual T.J. Martell Foundation New York Honors Gala, none of these stars were the headliner. Rather, it was the more than $3 million that the night&#8217;s attendees, who hailed from every corner of the music business, raised for the organization&#8217;s mission of cancer research.

Also above Matthews, Anastasio and Stapleton on the bill: Red Light Management founder Coran Capshaw , who represents all three musicians and received the lifetime music industry award at the event.

